a. humane treatment with attention to needs according to their age;

b. separation from adults;

c. provision of legal assistance and other assistance effectively;

d. implementation of recreational activities;

e. freedom from torture, punishment or other treatment that is cruel, inhumane and degrading to dignity and status;

f. avoidance of imposition of the death penalty and/or life imprisonment;

g. avoidance of detention or imprisonment, except as a last resort for the shortest possible time;

h. provision of justice before a Children's court that is objective, impartial, and in a closed hearing;

i. avoidance of publication of their identity;

j. provision of accompaniment by Parents/Guardians and persons trusted by the Child;

k. provision of social advocacy;

l. provision of private life;

m. provision of accessibility, especially for Children with Disabilities;

n. provision of education;

o. provision of health services; and

p. provision of other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 205

The community may play a role in the protection of Children in the following matters:

a. jointly and collectively ensuring that a Child whose parents are unable can continue their education according to their age;

b. providing opportunities for a Child to develop themselves by creating various learning programs outside of school according to the community's financial capacity;

c. protecting every Child from all disturbances and reductions to Children's rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

d. providing information through socialization and education regarding Children's Rights and laws and regulations concerning Children;

e. providing input in the formulation of policies related to Child Protection;

f. reporting to the competent authorities if violations of Children's rights occur;

g. playing an active role in the rehabilitation and social reintegration process for Children;

h. conducting monitoring, supervision and sharing responsibility for the implementation of Child Protection;

i. providing facilities and infrastructure and creating a conducive atmosphere for the growth and development of Children;

j. playing an active role by eliminating negative labeling of child victims; and

k. providing space for Children to participate and express their opinions.

