Article 199

Every parent who has Children has a primary role in the following matters:

a. caring for, maintaining, educating, and protecting Children to the maximum extent;

b. providing formal and informal education in accordance with the level and grade of education;

c. providing the widest possible opportunities and chances to Children who are members of their family to develop abilities in accordance with the interests and talents of the Child concerned;

d. providing correct guidance and understanding to Children in matters related to their religion and beliefs; and

e. teaching Children to behave in accordance with the ethics and customs prevailing in the midst of society.

Article 185

